WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:02.920
John: Good morning, Hank, it's Tuesday, in
a stunning turn of events, I have found myself

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:03.920
in an airport.

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.910
I'm here because I'm on my way to Brazil to
attend the Paper Towns premiere there, and

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:10.009
actually, I won't be returning home to my
beloved Indianapolis International Airport

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:16.230
for 28 days, except for a brief sojourn thanks
to the love and support of Nerdfighteria,

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:17.230
but more on that in a moment.

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:18.699
Alright, Hank, I have a bunch of news.

00:00:18.699 --> 00:00:21.679
First, bad news, my daughter Alice is a little
bit sick.

00:00:21.679 --> 00:00:25.070
She threw up this morning and it was just
horrible to watch, because in addition to

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:29.050
like, the regular miseries of throwing up,
children can't understand what's happening

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:32.200
to them, so she was just like, wait, why is
something coming out of my mouth, my mouth

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.530
is for putting things in!

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:37.000
But she doesn't have a very good vocabulary,
so she just kept saying 'noooo'.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.260
Oh, it was heartbreaking.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.370
Okay, Hank, on to some slightly better news.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:45.620
Cara Delevingne, Nat Wolff, Halston Sage,
and I are going on a brief tour of the United

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:47.250
States before the Paper Towns movie comes
out.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:51.450
Basically, everyone could vote for their state
on Tumblr, and the winning states were Ohio,

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:54.240
Texas, and my own home state of Indiana.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.530
Hank, it is not lost on me that Indiana is
a relatively small state that received a lot

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:02.400
of votes from kind people who do not live
here, but just thought that I might enjoy

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.330
having a day with my family, so thank you,
thank you, thank you.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.520
So, Hank, we'll be in Indianapolis July 14th,
Columbus, Ohio July 15th, and Dallas, Texas

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:16.760
July 16th, all the events are free, they will
be crazy fun, lots of surprises, I don't know

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.340
the venues and the times yet, but I should
sometime in the next week, I will let you

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:21.340
know.

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:23.980
In even more good news, last night, Sarah
and a bunch of my friends saw the Paper Towns

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:27.620
movie for the first time, and they all really
liked it, or else they're lying, but no, I

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.090
do think they really liked it.

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:30.950
They laughed, they felt things, it was good.

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:34.980
But in terrible news, literally none of them
noticed my cameo in the movie.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:38.650
I mean, Hank, at the end of the movie, my
life partner of more than a decade turned

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:40.810
to me and said, "That was such a great movie.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:42.420
I thought you said that you were in it.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:43.420
Where were you?"

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:46.090
So, yeah, Hank, I am in the movie, but apparently,
in a way that no one will notice.

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:47.210
Okay, even more good news.

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:50.300
Hank, the night before the Paper Towns movie
actually comes out in the United States on

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:54.420
July 24th, there will be a special event at
a couple hundred theaters on the night of

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:55.420
July 23rd.

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:59.260
That night of July 23rd is gonna be like the
first real public showing of the movie in

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:02.920
the US, and I'm so excited about it, and then
afterwards, there's gonna be this, like, livestream

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:07.750
beamed into theaters around the country featuring
the whole cast and also special guests I'm

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:08.750
not allowed to name.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:11.680
I'm just really excited to celebrate the movie
with the whole cast and with the people who

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.959
care the most about the story, so yeah, we're
gonna answer your questions and sing songs,

00:02:14.959 --> 00:02:18.829
it's gonna be tons of fun, nightonthetowns.com,
there's a link in the doobly-doo.

00:02:18.829 --> 00:02:22.439
Alright, Hank, now to the news that for many
years, I thought would be bad, but I think

00:02:22.439 --> 00:02:24.670
actually might turn out to be kind of great.

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:28.280
So Hank, more than 10 years ago, I sold the
movie rights to my first novel, Looking for

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:32.370
Alaska, and as you know, since then, I have
frequently tried to get them back.

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:35.859
Hank, there's a big part of me that never
wanted a Looking for Alaska movie to be made.

00:02:35.859 --> 00:02:39.469
The story is very personal to me, I know it
matters a lot to a lot of its readers, but

00:02:39.469 --> 00:02:43.279
then again, the money we made from selling
the movie rights was extremely important to

00:02:43.279 --> 00:02:46.560
us, it allowed us to move to New York so Sarah
could go to graduate school and pursue her

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.170
dream of becoming a curator.

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:51.189
So I could never really regret it, but as
you know, Hank, over the years, it's been

00:02:51.189 --> 00:02:53.950
difficult for me, I've had some mixed feelings
about it.

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:56.520
But Hank, suddenly it seems like the movie
isn't just going to happen, it's going to

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.639
happen in a way that I can be really proud
of.

00:02:58.639 --> 00:03:01.769
Weber and Neustadter, who also wrote the screenplays
for The Fault in Our Stars and Paper Towns

00:03:01.769 --> 00:03:06.079
have written a beautiful script and Becca
Thomas who previously directed the movie Electric

00:03:06.079 --> 00:03:11.129
Children has just been hired to direct Looking
for Alaska, and that means that it's probably

00:03:11.129 --> 00:03:12.129
gonna happen.

00:03:12.129 --> 00:03:15.160
It might still fall apart, things often do,
but now I hope that it doesn't, because I

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:19.409
really like Becca and she gets the book all
the way down.

00:03:19.409 --> 00:03:23.930
So yeah, I am excited about the prospect of
a Looking for Alaska movie are words I never

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:25.139
thought I would say, but I am.

00:03:25.139 --> 00:03:28.779
I hope you guys are excited too, and I hope
you're excited for the Paper Towns movie,

00:03:28.779 --> 00:03:32.709
I know that it's scary when a book is turned
into a movie, I mean, it's very scary for

00:03:32.709 --> 00:03:34.810
me, but it's exciting, too, so Hank, that's
the news.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:36.769
Oh wait, a couple more pieces of good news.

00:03:36.769 --> 00:03:40.260
The United State Supreme Court did not cancel
our health insurance, Hank, and also, no matter

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:44.900
who you are, and no matter where you live
in the United States, you can marry the person

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:45.900
you love.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:48.959
Here's to the activists and decades of activism
that made that happen.

00:03:48.959 --> 00:03:50.239
Hank, I'll see you on Friday.

00:03:50.239 --> 00:03:51.239
p.s.

00:03:51.239 --> 00:03:54.280
Hank, I tried to bring a champagne popper
into the airport so I could have a big huzzah

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:56.319
at the end of the video, but it turns out
that's not allowed.

